      "name": "Auer",
      "description": "Step into a time capsule of Geneva refinement where five generations of chocolatiers have upheld tradition since 1939. The warm-lit tea room hums with the quiet chatter of locals savoring morning cappuccinos and bite-sized Pignon cakes—delicate pine nut confections that draw a devoted following. Adjacent to the tea salon, the chocolatier counter becomes a pilgrimage site around Christmas when queues form for the legendary Amandes d'Auer, chocolate-covered almonds so celebrated they're simply called 'princess.' Retro 1970s decor anchors the space in classic Swiss elegance, making it ideal for leisurely afternoon tea, a genteel coffee break, or picking up Geneva's finest edible gifts. Expect mid-range pricing and an atmosphere where tradition tastes sweeter than trends.",
